# Generated by Cargo
# will have compiled files and executables
debug
target
target-*/

# Stray compilation output from invoking rustc directly on a single module
# (outside cargo, so no target dir catches it). These embed absolute source
# paths, so a committed one would leak local filesystem layout.
*.rlib

# These are backup files generated by rustfmt
**/*.rs.bk

# MSVC Windows builds of rustc generate these, which store debugging information
*.pdb

# Generated by cargo mutants
# Contains mutation testing data
**/mutants.out*/

# RustRover
#  JetBrains specific template is maintained in a separate JetBrains.gitignore that can
#  be found at https://github.com/github/gitignore/blob/main/Global/JetBrains.gitignore
#  and can be added to the global gitignore or merged into this file.  For a more nuclear
#  option (not recommended) you can uncomment the following to ignore the entire idea folder.
#.idea/

# Local scratch notes -- environment-specific, never commit
issues.md

# Captured live-traffic fixtures (raw, unsanitized bodies). Per-request
# directories under crates/routectl-cli/tests/fixtures/captured/ get
# auto-populated by scripts/capture_fixtures.sh from the TRACE log.
# Bodies contain user prompts AND model outputs -- never commit. The
# corpus is per-contributor and local-only by design; the repo ships
# the harness and the capture script, not the data.
crates/routectl-cli/tests/fixtures/captured/
# Driver-generated replay fixtures. Hermetic by construction (no real
# prompts), so unlike captured/ these are eligible for commit AND for
# gating. Gitignored while that committability call is still open --
# deleting THIS ONE LINE is the whole change when it is answered.
crates/routectl-cli/tests/fixtures/driver/
# Default landing root for scripts/capture_driver.sh. Exploratory driver
# runs write here, never straight into the corpus above: a rerun of a case
# overwrites that case's fixture, so a corpus default would replace a
# reviewed fixture in place. Fixtures reach the corpus only through
# scripts/promote_fixture.sh, which re-runs the scrub gate on the way in.
# Scratch by definition -- nothing here is ever committed.
.routectl-driver-scratch/
# Claude Code per-project session state (scheduled tasks, local
# settings, transient scratch). Never commit -- machine-specific.
.claude/

# Local research scratch -- personal notes, config references, experiments.
scratch/
.cargo-target-*/

# Default output dir for scripts/bench.sh baseline records, plus the
# per-run hermetic scratch it creates on real disk. Baselines that matter
# are archived out-of-repo by the operator; these are throwaway.
bench-results/
.routectl-bench-work/

# Per-run scratch for the image layer credential scan self-test: an
# extracted `docker save` tree, hundreds of MB, on real disk because /tmp
# here is a tmpfs a cold build already fills. Removed by the self-test's
# own exit trap; the ignore rule covers a run killed mid-scan.
.routectl-image-scan-work/
